    "quote": "For any algorithm, there exists a Bayesian decision-making task with a finite decision set and a single context ($\\abs{\\mathcal{C}=1}$) such that the regret can be lower bounded by $\\Omega(\\sqrt{\\abs{\\Pi}T})$."
